.TH STRTOK 3CRUNCH
.SH NAME
strtok \- split a string into tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <string.h>
.PP
.BI "char *strtok(char *" text ", const char *" delimiters );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The first call passes a writable string in
.IR text .
The function skips leading delimiter bytes and returns the next nonempty token,
replacing its terminating delimiter with a null byte.
Subsequent calls pass a null
.I text
to continue scanning. The delimiter set may change between calls.
A non-null
.I text
starts a new sequence.
.SH RETURN VALUE
A pointer to the next token, or NULL if no tokens remain.
.SH NOTES
The function uses shared internal state and is not reentrant or thread-safe.
Use
.BR strtok_r (3)
for independently managed state.
